From: Mira <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] never draw a pointer cursor

Mira is driven from the sofa. Its remote (a Rii i25, and air-mouse remotes
generally) sends OK as a left click, so the pointer device must stay alive and
its events must keep reaching Flutter - but a cursor drifting across a TV is
not part of the product, and Mira acts on the focused item rather than on
whatever the pointer happens to be over.

The app cannot do this from its side: Flutter's mouse cursor channel can ask
for the "none" kind, but flutter-pi re-enables the cursor on every pointer
motion, so it comes straight back.

--- a/src/flutter-pi.c
+++ b/src/flutter-pi.c
@@ -1713,8 +1713,12 @@
 
     flutterpi = userdata;
     (void) flutterpi;
+    (void) enabled;
 
-    compositor_set_cursor(flutterpi->compositor, true, enabled, false, POINTER_KIND_NONE, false, VEC2F(0, 0));
+    /* Mira: a TV has no cursor. Pointer devices stay enabled - the remote's OK
+     * button is a left click - but nothing is drawn for them.
+     */
+    compositor_set_cursor(flutterpi->compositor, true, false, false, POINTER_KIND_NONE, false, VEC2F(0, 0));
 }
 
 static void on_move_cursor(void *userdata, struct vec2f delta) {
@@ -1722,7 +1726,11 @@
 
     flutterpi = userdata;
 
-    compositor_set_cursor(flutterpi->compositor, true, true, false, POINTER_KIND_NONE, true, delta);
+    /* Mira: keep following the pointer so clicks land where Flutter expects,
+     * but leave it hidden. Upstream passes enabled=true here, which is what
+     * defeats asking for the "none" cursor kind from the Flutter side.
+     */
+    compositor_set_cursor(flutterpi->compositor, true, false, false, POINTER_KIND_NONE, true, delta);
 }
 
 static int on_user_input_open(const char *path, int flags, void *userdata) {
